<article class="env-lemma" id="042X">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/042X">Lemma <span data-tag="042X">8.5.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $\mathcal{S}_1$, $\mathcal{S}_2$ be categories over $\mathcal{C}$. Suppose that $\mathcal{S}_1$ and $\mathcal{S}_2$ are equivalent as categories over $\mathcal{C}$. Then $\mathcal{S}_1$ is a stack in groupoids over $\mathcal{C}$ if and only if $\mathcal{S}_2$ is a stack in groupoids over $\mathcal{C}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows by combining Lemmas <a href="/tag/02ZJ" data-tag="02ZJ">8.5.2</a> and <a href="/tag/042W" data-tag="042W">8.4.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>